A||N||6||Ozzy||Bad craftsmanship....ARGGHHHHHH!!!||||8||
Z||000000||Ozzy||04-02-2000||12:13 AM||||Hi Guys...<P>Been working on my GT today. Had to remove forward exhaust manifold, (that was FUN!)also entire exhaust system. <P>Anyway, as I started to look around under this thing up on stands I started noticing all of the 'little' things that are less than perfect.<P>It seems the guy that owned this car before me was another 'fixitqwik' sorta guy.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> The exhaust stud on bottom far right was not even in!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> (too hard I guess). The starter inspection cover is missing, 1 bolt missing from clutch inspection plate allowing it to swing down. This has allowed the tranny oil (leaking seal) to get into the clutch area! I guess I know why it slips in 5 gear huh?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> 30,000 zip ties all over the engine, bare hot wires floating around the starter, CAT. has been welded along with the exhaust mounting brackets! This made for an interesting removal technique acompanied by some colorful language. Ox. sensor has been crimp connectorized instead of replacing the disconnect plug... lottsa other stuff mostly small.<P>I don't want to get off on a rant here but...(Thank you Dennis Miller!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) <P>It just irritates the snot outta me when people do easyfix short cut work. This stuff only comes back to bite you later. I do some temporary things granted, but it gets where I can't sleep if I don't fix it right. Especially on these cars!!<P>The other part of this is that it just ticks me of to see all of the gerry rigging that goes on on the Fiero's I've seen up close. These cars don't deserve that do they??<P>Anyway, just had to vent a little. As soon as I can find a house that has a garage, I've decided I'm gonna drop the craddle out and clean this thing up right. It is filthy from years of grunge and leaking oil. I can then make plans to do all of the bushings, clutch, yada, yada, yada!!!<P>Ozzy<P><p>[This message has been edited by Ozzy (edited 04-02-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||mshill||04-02-2000||09:20 PM||||Ozzy,  I feel the same way, but I wouldn't have got such a good deal on my $500 86GT if the guy and his "mechanic" weren't so cheap.<P>The clutch had 10K miles on it and he didn't understand why it wouldn't shift well.  I took one look at it and found that it had a broken slave mount that was jerry-rigged (moving the slave back 1/8 inch), leaky master which they fixed by cutting/threading the plunger rod and putting a turnbuckle type  spacer on it to get more pedal travel.  What a mess, but easilty fixed with a good slave and bracket from the junkyard and a rebuilt master tht I had laying around.<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000002||Ozzy||04-02-2000||10:44 PM||||Hey ms'...<P>Yeah I suppose I got some 'bargaining power' 'cause of all things wrong too but it just amazes me to some of the easiest stuff to do still get jacked up with duct tape & twine!<P>Anyway, I will fix it all in time and all will be well with the world!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000003||sully5||04-02-2000||10:55 PM||||Ozzy, I feel for ya. I'm in just about the same position with mine. I figure that about the time I get everything squared away I will have basically done close to a full restoration on it. I am grateful that I am finally in a position that I can do things right, even if it means that the car is down for a few days. I just keep telling myself that it will be worth it in the long run.||||reg||1
Z||000004||sdm1964||04-03-2000||09:55 PM||||OK, so i read this post this morning and really ate into me as i went out to work on my new 86 SE. It has a blown head gasget and was just going to pull the heads. The more i was out there the more this post ate at me. SO now i have the complete crade on the ground, ready to clean, fix the heads , paint etc, etc. Boy you guys really know how to eat at a person. This was the first time a have ever pulled a crade out. went real well considering i was by myself, took all day but in the long run will be worth it. So plaes keep the heat off of me i am doing it right  OK!!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000005||fieroshop||04-03-2000||10:07 PM||||Hey OZZIE, your parts were shipped today and hopefully you will have them by thie weekend.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ozzy||04-04-2000||12:32 AM||||Right arm SDM1964! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Not that it was my intention to get anyone else goin'... just me lettin' of a little steam. But yeah, it WILL be worth it. <P>Hey George (FieroShop) Thnx for your help guy...I'm looking forward to getting my blue beast on the road! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
